
# --- Keeping secrets out of the environment (#126) -------------------------------
# Every variable below that holds a secret VALUE also accepts:
#   <NAME>_FILE=/path/to/file            contents are the secret (Docker/K8s secrets)
#   $CREDENTIALS_DIRECTORY/<NAME>        a systemd credential (LoadCredential=)
# The variable itself WINS if both are set, so nothing changes on upgrade — which also
# means an entry here silently shadows a _FILE you add later. Delete the line to switch.
# A named-but-unreadable source refuses the boot rather than falling back to no secret.
# Heldar deploy — copy to `.env` (or let install.sh generate one). The base OPEN stack (compose.yml)
# runs fine with NO .env: LAN defaults, auth off, plaintext at rest — appropriate for a trusted network.
# For production, use compose.prod.yml and set the values below. See docs/PRODUCTION.md.

# Pin an image version instead of :latest (recommended for production). e.g. 0.2.0
# HELDAR_VERSION=latest

# --- Production (read by compose.prod.yml / when auth is on) ---
# Master key for camera-credential encryption at rest — base64 of 32 bytes.
#   openssl rand -base64 32
# HELDAR_SECRET_KEY=

# Lock CORS to your dashboard origin(s), comma-separated. Empty = same-origin only.
# HELDAR_CORS_ORIGINS=
